Make diff find the file in a directory operand by its Windows base name.
When one operand is a directory, diff compares the other operand with
the file of the same name in that directory, taking the name after the
last '/'. On Windows a path such as sub\f.txt or c:f.txt has no '/', so
diff looked for dir/sub\f.txt or dir/c:f.txt and failed. Use
bb_basename(), which also splits at '\' and ':' on Windows and is the
same strrchr() on other platforms.

---
 editors/diff.c |    3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/editors/diff.c
+++ b/editors/diff.c
@@ -1108,8 +1108,7 @@
 		bool dirfile = S_ISDIR(stb[0].st_mode) || S_ISDIR(stb[1].st_mode);
 		bool dir = S_ISDIR(stb[1].st_mode);
 		if (dirfile) {
-			const char *slash = strrchr(file[!dir], '/');
-			file[dir] = concat_path_file(file[dir], slash ? slash + 1 : file[!dir]);
+			file[dir] = concat_path_file(file[dir], bb_basename(file[!dir]));
 			xstat(file[dir], &stb[dir]);
 		}
 		/* diffreg can get non-regular files here */
